# Coding Standards and Style Guidelines

## CSS Standards

### File Organization
- **All CSS changes** go in `static/assets/css/user.css`
- **Organize sections** with clear header comments
- **Group related styles** together
- **Use consistent** indentation (2 spaces)

### CSS Naming Conventions
```css
/* Use descriptive, component-based names */
.student-dashboard { }
.reading-log-form { }
.progress-mini { }
.chart-container-small { }

/* Avoid generic names */
.box { } /* ❌ Not descriptive */
.thing { } /* ❌ Not descriptive */
```

### Dark/Light Mode CSS
```css
/* Always provide both modes */
.component {
    background-color: #ffffff;
    color: #212529;
}

html.dark .component {
    background-color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.05);
    color: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.9);
}
```

### CSS Performance
- **Use efficient selectors** (avoid deep nesting)
- **Minimize** `!important` usage
- **Group** media queries
- **Use** CSS custom properties for theme values

## JavaScript Standards

### Function Organization
```javascript
// Check theme.js first for existing functions
// Use descriptive function names
function loadStudentProgress(studentId) {
    // Implementation
}

function updateReadingLogTable(data) {
    // Implementation
}

// Avoid generic names
function doStuff() { } // ❌ Not descriptive
```

### AJAX Patterns
```javascript
// Use consistent error handling
fetch('/api/endpoint')
    .then(response => response.json())
    .then(data => {
        if (data.success) {
            // Handle success
        } else {
            showAlert('error', data.message);
        }
    })
    .catch(error => {
        console.error('Error:', error);
        showAlert('error', 'An error occurred');
    });
```

### Event Handling
```javascript
// Use consistent event listener patterns
document.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function() {
    // Initialize components
    initializeDashboard();
    setupEventListeners();
});

function setupEventListeners() {
    // Group related listeners
    document.getElementById('save-btn').addEventListener('click', saveData);
    document.getElementById('cancel-btn').addEventListener('click', cancelEdit);
}
```

## Django Code Standards

### View Patterns
```python
from django.contrib.auth.decorators import login_required
from django.shortcuts import get_object_or_404

@login_required
def student_detail(request, student_id):
    # Always filter by user permissions
    if request.user.user_type == 'teacher':
        student = get_object_or_404(
            Student,
            id=student_id,
            classrooms__teachers=request.user
        )
    elif request.user.user_type == 'parent':
        student = get_object_or_404(
            Student,
            id=student_id,
            parents=request.user
        )
    # ... handle other user types
```

### Model Standards
```python
class ReadingLog(models.Model):
    # Use descriptive field names
    student = models.ForeignKey(Student, on_delete=models.CASCADE)
    book_title = models.CharField(max_length=200)
    pages_read = models.PositiveIntegerField()
    reading_time_minutes = models.PositiveIntegerField()
    
    class Meta:
        ordering = ['-created_at']
        
    def __str__(self):
        return f"{self.student.name} - {self.book_title}"
```

### Form Standards
```python
class ReadingLogForm(forms.ModelForm):
    class Meta:
        model = ReadingLog
        fields = ['book_title', 'author', 'pages_read', 'reading_time_minutes']
        widgets = {
            'book_title': forms.TextInput(attrs={'class': 'form-control'}),
            'pages_read': forms.NumberInput(attrs={'class': 'form-control', 'min': '0'}),
        }
    
    def __init__(self, *args, **kwargs):
        self.user = kwargs.pop('user', None)
        super().__init__(*args, **kwargs)
        
        # Filter choices based on user permissions
        if self.user and self.user.user_type == 'teacher':
            self.fields['student'].queryset = self.user.teacher_students.all()
```

## Template Standards

### Template Organization
```django
{% extends "general/nav_template.html" %}
{% load static %}

{% block title %}Page Title{% endblock %}

{% block content %}
<!-- Main content -->
{% endblock %}

{% block afterScripts %}
<!-- Page-specific JavaScript -->
{% endblock %}
```

### Conditional Rendering
```django
<!-- Use clear permission checks -->
{% if user.user_type == 'teacher' %}
    <button class="btn btn-primary">Edit Student</button>
{% elif user.user_type == 'administrator' %}
    <button class="btn btn-danger">Delete Student</button>
{% endif %}

<!-- Group related permissions -->
{% if user.user_type in 'teacher,administrator' %}
    <!-- Teacher and admin content -->
{% endif %}
```

### Form Templates
```django
<form method="post">
    {% csrf_token %}
    
    <div class="row">
        <div class="col-md-6">
            <div class="mb-3">
                <label for="{{ form.book_title.id_for_label }}" class="form-label">
                    {{ form.book_title.label }}
                </label>
                {{ form.book_title }}
                {% if form.book_title.errors %}
                    <div class="invalid-feedback d-block">
                        {{ form.book_title.errors.0 }}
                    </div>
                {% endif %}
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
    
    <button type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">Save</button>
</form>
```

